  "notes": "{高揚|こうよう}する functions as a suru-verb meaning \"to rise\" or \"to be uplifted.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {気分|きぶん}が{高揚|こうよう}する (spirits rise)\n- {士気|しき}が{高揚|こうよう}する (morale is boosted)\n- {高揚|こうよう}{感|かん} (feeling of elation)\n- ナショナリズムの{高揚|こうよう} (rise of nationalism)\n- {意識|いしき}の{高揚|こうよう} (heightening of awareness)\n\nNot to be confused with the homophone {紅葉|こうよう} (autumn leaves). {高揚|こうよう} describes emotional or psychological elevation. A somewhat formal word, more commonly seen in writing than in casual speech.",
